    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nWith cover_or_* search methods, the single-line pass can return a non-covering match before the multi-line pass gets to run, even when a covering match spanning multiple lines exists.\n\nExample with cursor on |:\n```lua\nvim.notify(table.concat(vim.|iter(items)\n  :map(tostring)\n  :totable(), '\\n'))\n```\n\nvi( selects inside iter(...) (next on cursor line) instead of inside table.concat(...) (multi-line cover). The multi-line pass never runs because the single-line pass already found a result.\n\nProposed solution:\nAn opt-in option to prevent a non-covering same-line match from satisfying the search when a multi-line covering match may exist.\n",
